{%- comment -%}
  Three Bargain Bin picks at the foot of the mobile menu.

  THE BIN, NOT THE YOINK, and the reason is placement economics rather than
  taste. The Yoink is already the most-surfaced thing on this site: the
  announcement bar carries it on EVERY page, it is the homepage hero, and the
  nav points at it. Anybody who opened this drawer scrolled past it to get
  here. The Bargain Bin has one nav link and one homepage section, so the menu
  is the cheapest place to give it a second surface.

  Margin agrees. The Yoink is priced near cost — measured at $3.30 a unit on 4
  August against a $15.00 cost — while bin members sit above a 20% margin floor
  at a flat 25% off. A drawer is a conversion surface, so it should carry the
  thing that makes money rather than the thing that makes the brand.

  And a menu is opened by somebody who did NOT find what they wanted. Varied,
  cheap, impulse-shaped items are exactly right for that moment; one expensive
  deal they have already declined is not.

  RANKED BY DOLLAR SAVING, which is the ranking the weekly email had to learn
  the hard way. The bin is a FLAT 25%, so every member ties on percentage and
  the sort collapses to whatever the tie-break is — breaking toward cheapest
  put two colourways of one ball holder and "NUDE MALE BODY FIGURINE #2" in the
  first weekly. At a fixed percentage the biggest saving is simply the most
  expensive item, so sorting by price descending gets it for free.

  ONE PER TITLE FAMILY. Collective syncs colourways as separate products, and
  three cards showing the same object twice reads as a bin with nothing in it.
  Keyed on the title before the first dash, which is where every supplier in
  this catalogue puts the variant name.

  `no-promo` is honoured here too. The bin is curated on margin, not on whether
  something belongs in a shop window, and this is a shop window.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # LIQUID DOES NOT ALLOW A FILTER INSIDE A BRACKET LOOKUP. Written as
  # `collections[handle | default: 'bargain-bin']` this resolves to nil, the
  # guard below fails, and the snippet renders absolutely nothing — silently,
  # with no error anywhere. Resolve the handle first, then index with it.
  #
  # `collection_handle` rather than `handle`, because `handle` is a global on
  # product and collection templates and a snippet parameter that shadows a
  # global is a bug waiting for a different page.
  assign picks_handle = collection_handle | default: 'bargain-bin'
  assign bin = collections[picks_handle]
  assign want = count | default: 3
-%}

{%- if bin != blank and bin.products_count > 0 -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign ranked = bin.products | sort: 'price' | reverse
    assign seen = ''
    assign taken = 0
  -%}

  <div class="aj-picks">
    {%- if heading != blank -%}
      <p class="aj-picks__heading">{{ heading }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <ul class="aj-picks__grid" role="list">
      {%- for product in ranked -%}
        {%- if taken >= want -%}
          {%- break -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- liquid
          assign tags_joined = product.tags | join: ','
          assign family = product.title | split: '-' | first | split: '|' | first | strip | downcase
          assign skip = false
          if tags_joined contains 'no-promo'
            assign skip = true
          endif
          if seen contains family
            assign skip = true
          endif
        -%}

        {%- unless skip -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign seen = seen | append: family | append: '||'
            assign taken = taken | plus: 1
            assign v = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
            assign saving = 0
            if v.compare_at_price > v.price
              assign saving = v.compare_at_price | minus: v.price
            endif
          -%}
          <li class="aj-picks__item">
            <a class="aj-picks__tile" href="{{ product.url }}">
              <span class="aj-picks__media">
                {%- if product.featured_media -%}
                  {{
                    product.featured_media
                    | image_url: width: 300
                    | image_tag:
                      loading: 'lazy',
                      widths: '120, 200, 300',
                      sizes: '30vw',
                      class: 'aj-picks__image',
                      alt: product.title
                  }}
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
              <span class="aj-picks__name">{{ product.title | escape }}</span>
              <span class="aj-picks__price">
                {{ v.price | money }}
                {%- if saving > 0 -%}
                  <s class="aj-picks__was">{{ v.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endunless -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>

    {%- if link_text != blank -%}
      <a class="aj-picks__all" href="{{ bin.url }}">
        {{- link_text -}}
        <span aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;&rarr;</span>
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
